  "observations": {
    "growth": "Single flat sticky-note face becomes overlapping connected notes, then a broad layered keeper. The living sheet identity persists through evolution. No animal/dragon muzzle, long neck, horns or tail remains.",
    "eyes": "The larger40pixelJotlet and48pixelMemofold fronts retain separate black eyes and white windows. Recallisk54 has a central face distinct from its surrounding stacks. Native eyes need not retain every source highlight fleck.",
    "hands": "Recallisk has two separate folded square sheet hands facing forward; Memofold has readable side sheet arms. No extra animal limbs are introduced.",
    "outline": "Selected solid exterior closes the pale outer highlights and curled-page corners more continuously than source-backed comparison, with stepped edges and distinct fold gaps.",
    "backs": "All three are independent close upper-rear portraits with blank reverse sides, matching large curled/adhesive top edges, stage colors and layered sheet anatomy. They do not introduce a second rear face or shrink a full creature into the back frame.",
    "palettes": "Exact four inks per species, matching approved white/yellow/brown, white/pink/mauve and white/cream/mint RGB555 words. Front/back share only their own species palette.",
    "source_consistency": "All six selected native views retain the source arrangement, central faces, large fold forms and color assignment. Quantization necessarily simplifies small source glints/texture into native clusters.",
    "page_count_limit": "The design target is1/3/7notes. Overlapping folds expose tabs/reverse planes, so a unique unfolded sheet count is not provable from these opaque sprites; this review accepts the visible single-note\u2192connected-note\u2192large-keeper growth rather than claiming a mechanically audited page count."
  },
